What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/10004000.vcorefs/state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Read-only PCM ownership, physical PHY shuffle, decoded DDR data
		rate (MT/s), AXI clock (Hz), baseline shuffle, successful changes
		and failures. CPU voltage ownership remains with CPUfreq.
		The standard devfreq userspace set_freq interface selects nominal
		DRAM clocks in Hz; a selection succeeds only after the physical
		PHY and PCM both acknowledge it. A timeout is not a low-rate PASS.
		This board exposes 800000000 and 635000000 requests. The
		uncompleted 400000000 ULPM transition is excluded from the OPPs;
		it is a recorded implementation limitation, not a qualified level.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/10004000.vcorefs/release
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Write 1 to restore the initial memory level, offload and reset
		the PCM before releasing instruction DMA, restore the saved
		SPM/PWRAP/PMIC and AXI state, and drop the firmware module hold.
		MEM/DFS_MEM DCM preserves the current user's latched settings.
		If hardware does not stop, the firmware buffer and module remain
		held and the write fails. A subsequent set_freq starts it again.
